invariant: INV-16
file: p256_wide_field.c
catches: proof/prove-one.sh p256_wide_field
reason: the multiple of p's top limb loses the subtraction that keeps its
  high limb at or under 2^64 - 2^32, so that limb is u itself and adding
  the carry of the round before wraps when u is 2^64 - 1. uint64_t
  defines the wrap, so nothing faults and the round drops 2^64.
  proof/p256_wide_field_harness.c runs reduce() under
  --unsigned-overflow-check, which makes that sum a property. Each run is
  a proof, so this belongs to the nightly's test-invariants-proof-backed
  job.

--- old
    uint64_t multiple_high = p256_wide_sub_borrow(&borrow, u, u >> 32);
--- new
    uint64_t multiple_high = u;
